PART 5 — BADGE AND ADMINISTRATIVE AUTHORITY
==================================================

This is a critical part of the platform.

There are three visible badge types.

A. SUPREME ADMIN

Appearance:
Purple, thick, shiny and visually distinctive.

This represents the highest ordinary platform administrator authority.

B. MODERATOR

Appearance:
Red badge.

Moderators are appointed by Supreme Admin.

Moderator powers:

- Delete ordinary members' posts.
- Delete ordinary members' anonymous posts and anonymous replies.
- Moderate ordinary members' comments and replies.
- Approve ordinary members' marketplace listings.
- Perform the permitted content-management operations assigned to moderators.

Moderator restrictions:

- Cannot reveal anonymous identities.
- Cannot suspend accounts.
- Cannot grant, remove or change badges.
- Cannot manage other administrator accounts.
- Cannot delete or alter content belonging to Verified users.
- Cannot delete or alter content belonging to other Moderators.
- Cannot change the role of another user.
- Cannot remove a Verified or Moderator badge.
- Cannot override Supreme Admin authority.

Moderator content deletions are permanent.

C. VERIFIED

Appearance:
Green badge.

Verified users can publish ordinary community updates.

They can:

- Publish updates.
- Comment.
- Reply.
- Like content.
- Participate in permitted platform activities.

They cannot:

- Delete other people's content.
- Moderate other members.
- Approve marketplace listings on behalf of administrators.
- Grant or remove badges.
- Manage accounts.

BADGE MANAGEMENT:

Only Supreme Admin can:

- Grant Verified badges.
- Remove Verified badges.
- Grant Moderator badges.
- Remove Moderator badges.
- Promote a Verified user to Moderator.
- Manage administrator accounts and permissions.

A Moderator cannot manage another Moderator or Verified account.

A Supreme Admin can moderate content from every account, including Moderators and Verified users.

