PART 6 — HIDDEN PLATFORM OWNER AND CUSTOMER ADMINISTRATOR
==================================================

The system must support a permanent platform owner account and a separate customer administrator account.

PLATFORM OWNER:

The original developer is the platform owner.

The owner must:

- Have the highest backend authority.
- Be able to access the administrator dashboard.
- Be able to perform all administrative operations.
- Be able to grant and revoke badges.
- Be able to manage customer administrator permissions.
- Be protected against removal or demotion by another administrator.

The owner should not appear in the ordinary public member directory or customer-facing administrator directory.

The owner account must remain a real authenticated account, not a fake hidden user.

CUSTOMER ADMINISTRATOR:

The customer receives a Supreme Admin account.

The customer can manage the platform according to Supreme Admin permissions.

The customer must not be able to remove, demote or take ownership of the permanent platform owner account.

The owner and customer administrator must be separate authenticated accounts.

Do not invent the customer's email address.

Do not create fake customer credentials.

The customer's account will be added when their real email is available.

SECURITY REQUIREMENT:

Use trusted server-side role management.

Use Firebase Admin SDK custom claims or another secure server-side role mechanism supported by the project.

Never let frontend JavaScript assign administrator privileges.

Never allow a user to grant themselves Supreme Admin, Moderator or Verified status.

If a secure owner-bootstrap procedure requires manual action, explain exactly what is required. Never create an insecure public endpoint that allows the first person to register to become administrator.

The owner's hidden directory status must not be confused with actual security. Enforce owner protection in the backend.

