SECURITY RULE PRINCIPLES:

Default deny.

Only allow operations that are explicitly permitted.

Users must not read another user's private account information.

Users must not modify another user's profile.

Users must not change their own roles or badges.

Ordinary members must not publish ordinary community feed posts.

Only permitted roles can publish ordinary feed updates.

Only permitted administrators can publish opportunities and events.

Marketplace approval must follow the permission hierarchy.

Moderators must not alter Verified or Moderator accounts or their content.

Only Supreme Admin can reveal anonymous identities.

Anonymous identity mappings must never be publicly readable.

No user may grant themselves administrator privileges.

No public client-side operation may grant badges.

Do not use rules that simply allow all authenticated users to read and write everything.

Do not use broad wildcard permissions as a shortcut.

Do not rely on hidden buttons as a security measure.

The database itself must enforce permissions.

Use server-side validation for privileged operations.

Create a documented permission matrix so every role's capabilities are clear.

